

#====================================================#
#  CASE INPUT DATA <ARRAKIS> $2.0                    #
#====================================================#


#====================================================#
TIME PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  MAXIMAL NUMBER OF ITERATIONS [int]                 : 10000000
  Code variable: nitermax
  Maximum number of iteration for time loop

  DURATION [float]                                   : 100.
  Code variable: time_max
  Final time of the simulation in second

  TIME STEP [float]                                  : 1.
  Code variable: dt_const
  if variable time step:
  - specified value is ignored (use CFL NUMBER instead)
  - only used for the frequency of output writing
  
  VARIABLE TIME STEP [bool]                          : yes
  Code variable: var_dt
  no : constant time step
  yes: variable time step
  Remark: If yes: TIME STEP is only used for graphic printouts
  
  CFL NUMBER [float]                                 : 0.9
  Code variable: cfl
  CFL condition for VARIABLE TIME STEP = yes
  Time step is computed as: dt = CFL*dx/lambda

  PARALLEL EXECUTION [bool]                          : yes
  Code variable: use_omp
  Run in parallel mode with OpenMP


#====================================================#
OUTPUT PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  RESULT FILE [str]                                  : RES
  Code variable: res_file
  Name of the result file

  LISTING FREQUENCY [int]                            : 1
  Code variable: ndisplay
  Frequency of listing printouts
  If LISTING FREQUENCY = 1: prints once every TIME STEP

  OUTPUT FREQUENCY [int]                             : 1
  Code variable: nrecord
  Frequency of output writing
  If LISTING FREQUENCY = 1: prints once every TIME STEP

  VARIABLES [str]                                    : ZB,H,U
  Code variable: vars_outputs
  ZB : bottom elevation [m]
  ZS : water surface elevation [m]
  H  : water depth [m]
  U  : water velocity [m/s]
  Q  : water discharge [m^2/s]
  QL : water volumic discharge, QL = Q*L [m^3/s]
  L  : rectangular channel width [m]
  CI : finite volume cell size [m]
  RH : hydraulic radius [m]
  FR : Froude number [-]
  FC : friction coefficient [-]
  B  : sediment depth [m]
  ZF : hard ground elevation [m]
  QS : solid discharge [m^2/s]
  QSL: solid volumic discharge [m^3/s]
  TB : bottom shear stress (tau) [Pa]
  TS : dimensionless bottom shear stress (tau*)
  A  : wetted area, A=H*L [m^2]
  V  : water volume in each cell, V=H*L*ci [m^3]
  AS : sediment area, AS=b*L [m^2]
  VS : sediment volume, VS=b*L*ci [m^3]
  Ti : tracer number i (1<=i<=99) [-]
  CE : suspension equilibirum concentration [kg/m^3]
  WS : settling velocity [m/s]
  RO : Rouse number [-]
  A1 : auxiliary array 1 (for debug) [-]
  A2 : auxiliary array 2 (for debug) [-]

  PROBES [int]                                       : 0
  Code variable: probes
  Number of probes

  PROBES COORDINATES [float]                         : 0.
  Code variable: probes_x
  Coordinates of probes

  PROBES VARIABLES [str]                             : H
  Code variable: vars_probes
  Variables to printout in probe files 
  Remark: see VARIABLES names

  PROBES FILE NAME                                   : PROBE
  Code variable: pbr_file
  Name of probe file

  PROBES FREQUENCY [int]                             : 0
  Code variable: nrecord_probes
  0  : record probes and mass balance at every time step
  >0 : record every N time steps (same logic as OUTPUT FREQUENCY)

  SNAPSHOTS [int]                                    : 0
  Code variable: snaps
  Number of snapshots

  SNAPSHOTS TIMES [float]                            : 0.
  Code variable: snaps_t
  Snapshot times

  MASS BALANCE [bool]                                : no
  Code variable: mass_balance
  no : do not write mass balance file
  yes: write mass balance boundary flux time series file
  Output columns depend on MASS BALANCE OPTION (see below)

  MASS BALANCE OPTION [int]                          : 1
  Code variable: mb_option
  0: write FH, FQ, FQS
     columns: Time, FH_L, FQ_L, FQS_L, FH_R, FQ_R, FQS_R
  1: write QL and QSL
     QL  = FH*L   (water volumic discharge)
     QSL = FQS*L (solid volumic discharge)
     columns: Time, QL_L, QSL_L, QL_R, QSL_R

  MASS BALANCE FILE NAME [str]                       : MB
  Code variable: mb_file
  Name of mass balance output file


#====================================================#
MESH PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  NUMBER OF NODES [int]                              : 100
  Code variable: nx
  Number of nodes in mesh
  Remark: Ignored if MESH FILE = yes

  CHANNEL XA [float]                                 : 0.
  Code variable: xa
  Abscissa of left boundary
  Remark: Ignored if MESH FILE = yes

  CHANNEL XB [float]                                 : 10.
  Code variable: xb
  Abscissa of right boundary
  Remark: Ignored if MESH FILE = yes

  CHANNEL WIDTH [float]                              : 1.
  Code variable: Lcst
  constant width of the channel
  Remark: Ignored if VARIABLE CHANNEL WIDTH = yes

  HYDRAULIC RADIUS APPROXIMATION [int]               : 1
  Code variable: Rh_approx
  0: Rh = h
  1: Rh = h*B/(B + 2*h)
  Remark: Ignored if VARIABLE CHANNEL WIDTH = True

  MESH FILE [bool]                                   : no
  Code variable: use_mesh_file
  no : do not use mesh file
  yes: use mesh file 
  Remark: CHANNEL XA, XB and NUMBER OF NODES ignored
  
  MESH FILE NAME [str]                               : MESH
  Code variable: mesh_file
  Mesh file name
  Remark: file must have the extension .geo

  VARIABLE CHANNEL WIDTH [bool]                      : no
  Code variable: variable_width
  no : constant channel width, solves the SV1D eq.
  yes: varianle channel width, solves the SV1D eq. with
  variable rectangular cross section (new source terms)


#====================================================#
PHYSICAL PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  BOTTOM FRICTION LAW [int]                          : 0
  Code variable: frict_law
  Bottom friction law, available options:
  0:  None
  1:  Fanning
  2:  Chezy
  3:  Strickler (1981): ks/h in [0.007;0.1]
  4:  Nikuradse (1950): ks/h in [0;0.1]
  5:  Colebrook-White (1939): ks/h in [0;0.1]
  6:  Haaland (1983) : explicit version of CW (C=12)
  7:  Barr (1977)    : explicit version of CW (C=14.8)
  8:  Bathurst (1985): ks/h in [0.1;5.15]
  9:  Machiels (2011): Barr+Bathurst, ks/h in [0,5.15]
  10: Ferguson (2007):  ks/h in [0,1.]

  BOTTOM FRICTION COEFFICIENT [float]                : 0.
  Code variable: frict_coef
  Friction coefficient (unit depends on the law)

  DIFFUSION OF VELOCITY [bool]                       : no
  Code variable: diffusion_u
  no: No diffusion of velocity
  yes: diffusion of velocity

  VELOCITY DIFFUSIVITY [float]                       : 1.E-6
  Code variable: nu_u
  velocity diffusivity coefficient in m^2/s


#====================================================#
NUMERICAL PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  ADVECTION SCHEME [int]                             : 1
  Code variable: method
  1: Roe
  2: HLL (Harten Lax Van-Leer) 
  3: ACU (Audusse Chalon Ung)
  4: Kinetic (only SV)
  Remark: ignored if TIME SCHEME = 0 (steady kernel)

  TIME SCHEME [int]                                  : 1
  Code variable: time_scheme
  0: Steady
  1: Euler explicit (order 1)
  2: Heun (order 2)
  3: RK2 (order 2, experimental, only SV)
  4: RK3 (order 3, experimental, only SV)
  
  SPACE ORDER [int]                                  : 1
  Code variable: ordre
  1: first order
  2: second order
  3: third order (experimental)
  5: Fifth order WENO (experimental)

  SPACE ORDER FOR TRACERS [int]                      : 1
  Code variable: ordre_trac
  1: first order
  2: second order
  3: third order (experimental)
  5: Fifth order WENO (experimental)

  SVE SCHEME OPTION [int]                            : 0
  Code variable: swe_scheme_opt
  0: Coupled schemes (ROE-SVE, HLL-SVE or ACU-SVE)
     selected via ADVECTION SCHEME
  1: SV advection scheme + Exner Centered (unstable)
  2: SV advection scheme + Exner Upwind (c=dq/dzb)
  3: SV advection scheme + Exner Upwind (Fr)
  4: SV advection scheme + Exner HLL
  Remark: option only available for TIME SCHEME =! 0
  
  STD SCHEME OPTION [int]                            : 0
  Code variable: std_scheme_opt
  0: non-linear (Newton iterative solver)
  1: linearized equations
  Remark: option only available for TIME SCHEME = 0


#====================================================#
INITIAL CONDITION:
#====================================================#
  INITIAL FILE [bool]                                : no
  Code variable: use_ini_file
  no : dont use ini file
  yes: use ini file (INITIAL CONDITION ignored)
  Remark: zb defined from mesh file is ignored
  Remark: ini file must contain: x, zb, h, u
  Remark: ini file mesh nodes can be different,
  in which case linear interpolation is performed
  to get the solution on the current simulation mesh

  INITIAL FILE NAME [str]                            : INI
  Code variable: ini_file
  Remark: file must have the extension .ini

  INITIAL CONDITION [int]                            : 1
  Code variable: type_init
  0 : ALL NULL
  1 : CONSTANT ELEVATION and CONSTANT FLOWRATE
  2 : CONSTANT WATER DEPTH and CONSTANT FLOWRATE

  CONSTANT WATER DEPTH [float]                       : 1.
  Code variable: const_h

  CONSTANT ELEVATION [float]                         : 1.
  Code variable: const_e

  CONSTANT FLOWRATE [float]                          : 0.
  Code variable: const_q
  fluid discharge in m3/s


#====================================================#
BOUNDARY CONDITIONS:
#====================================================#
  ELEVATION OR WATER DEPTH FORMULATION [int]         : 1
  Code variable: clhorz
  0: free surface elevation
  1: water depth (default)
  (automatic detection if BND file is used)

  VELOCITY OR FLOWRATE FORMULATION [int]             : 1
  Code variable: clqoru
  0: velocity 
  1: flowrate (default)
  (automatic detection if BND file is used)

  LEFT BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]                      : 3
  Code variable: bctype_l
  1: Wall
  2: h imposed (Fluvial)
  3: q imposed (Fluvial)
  4: h and q imposed (Torrential)
  5: none imposed (Torrential)
  6: Neumann
  7: Periodic

  LEFT ELEVATION IMPOSED [float]                     : 1.
  Code variable: zsa
  
  LEFT DEPTH IMPOSED [float]                         : 1.
  Code variable: ha
  
  LEFT VELOCITY IMPOSED [float]                      : 0.1
  Code variable: ua
  
  LEFT FLOWRATE IMPOSED [float]                      : 0.1
  Code variable: qa
  fluid discharge in m3/s

  LEFT BOUNDARY FILE [bool]                          : no
  Code variable: use_bcfile_l
  no : liquid boundary file not used
  yes: liquid boundary file used, imposed values ignored
  LEFT BOUNDARY FILE NAME [str]                      : BCL
  Code variable: bcfile_l
  Remark: file must have the extension .liq

  RIGHT BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]                     : 2
  Code variable: bctype_r
  1: Wall
  2: h imposed (Fluvial)
  3: q imposed (Fluvial)
  4: h and q imposed (Torrential)
  5: none imposed (Torrential)
  6: Homogeneous Neumann (null gradients)
  7: Periodic

  RIGHT ELEVATION IMPOSED [float]                    : 1.
  Code variable: zsb
  
  RIGHT DEPTH IMPOSED [float]                        : 1.
  Code variable: hb
  
  RIGHT VELOCITY IMPOSED [float]                     : -0.1
  Code variable: ub
  
  RIGHT FLOWRATE IMPOSED [float]                     : -0.1
  Code variable: qb
  fluid discharge in m3/s

  RIGHT BOUNDARY FILE [bool]                         : no
  Code variable: use_bcfile_r
  no : liquid boundary file not used
  yes: liquid boundary file used, imposed values ignored
  RIGHT BOUNDARY FILE NAME [str]                     : BCR
  Code variable: bcfile_r
  Remark: file must have the extension .liq

  BOUNDARY CONDITION OPTION [int]                    : 0
  Code variable: bc_opt
  0: no extrapolation, no sources, no rec
  1: no extrapolation, sources, no rec
  2: extrapolation, sources, no rec
  3: extrapolation, sources, rec


#====================================================#
TRACER PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  NUMBER OF TRACERS [int]                            : 0
  Code variable: ntrac

  INITIAL TRACER VALUES                              : 0.
  Code variable: const_t

  LEFT TRACER BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]               : 1
  Code variable: bctypet_l
  1: Dirichlet (tracer value imposed)
  2: Homogeneous Neumann (null gradients)
  3: Periodic

  LEFT TRACER VALUE IMPOSED [float]                  : 0.
  Code variable: ta

  RIGHT TRACER BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]              : 1
  Code variable: bctypet_r
  1: Dirichlet (tracer value imposed)
  2: Homogeneous Neumann (null gradients)
  3: Periodic

  RIGHT TRACER VALUE IMPOSED [float]                 : 0.
  Code variable: tb

  DIFFUSION OF TRACERS [bool]                        : no
  Code variable: diffusion_t
  no: No diffusion of tracers
  yes: diffusion of tracers

  TRACER DIFFUSIVITY [float]                         : 1.E-6
  Code variable: nu_t


#====================================================#
SEDIMENT PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#
  BED POROSITY [float]                               : 0.25
  Code variable: porosite
  
  SEDIMENT DENSITY [float]                           : 2650.
  Code variable: rhos
  
  SEDIMENT D50 [float]                               : 2.E-3
  Code variable: d50

  SEDIMENT D16 [float]                               : 0.
  Code variable: d16
  Only for Lefort bedload law
  if 0.: auto-compute as 0.5*d50 

  SEDIMENT DM [float]                                : 0.
  Code variable: dm
  Only for Lefort and Recking bedload laws
  if 0.: auto-compute as 1.1*d50 

  SEDIMENT D84 [float]                               : 0.
  Code variable: d84
  Only for Lefort and Recking bedload laws
  if 0.: auto-compute as 2.1*d50

  ACTIVATE SUSPENSION [bool]                         : no
  Code variable: suspension
  no : no suspended sediments
  yes: activate suspended sediments

  SUSPENSION FORMULA [int]                           : 2
  Code variable: suspension_formula
  1: From qs computed with BEDLOAD FORMULA
  2: Engelund and Hansen (1967)
  3: Van Rijn (1984)
  4: Zyserman-Fredsoe (1994)

  SUSPENSION CALIBRATION COEFFICIENT [float]         : 1.
  Code variable: suspension_coef

  SUSPENSION SETTLING VELOCITY [float]               : 0.
  Code variable: ws_susp
  - if == 0.: computed in Arrakis as a function of d50
  - if != 0.: user defined constant value

  SUSPENSION USE ROUSE PROFILE [bool]                : no
  Code variable: rouse_profile
  yes : use Rouse profile to compute Czref = C*csratio
  no : do not use use Rouse profile, Czref = C

  SUSPENSION CRITICAL STABILIZATION [bool]           : no
  Code variable: susp_critdiff
  Add artificial diffusivity to stabilize the solution
  in critical flows 

  SUSPENSION CRITICAL STABILIZATION COEFFICIENT [f]  : 0.2
  Code variable: susp_nu_u
  coefficient of additional velocity diffusivity
  (nu_tot = nu_u + coef*fr**2)

  ACTIVATE BEDLOAD [bool]                            : no
  Code variable: bedload
  no : no bedload (SV equation)
  yes: activate bedload (SVE equations)

  LEFT BEDLOAD BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]              : 2
  Code variable: bctypeqs_l
  1: Dirichlet (qs imposed : in m3/s
     * fixed value by keyword LEFT SOLID FLUX or by
     * additional column QS in LEFT BOUNDARY FILE)
  2: Homogeneous Neumann (null gradients)
  3: Periodic
  4: Equilibrium slope (qs = f(Jeq))
  5: Dirichlet (qs computed from hydro cdl values)

  LEFT SOLID FLUX [float]                            : 0.
  Code variable: qsa
  Imposed solid flux qs (for Dirichlet condition: 1)
  solid discharge in m3/s

  LEFT EQUILIBRIUM SLOPE [float]                     : 0.005
  Code variable: Jeqa
  Imposed equilibrium slope Jep (for bnd condition :4)

  RIGHT BEDLOAD BOUNDARY CONDITION [int]             : 2
  Code variable: bctypeqs_r
  1: Dirichlet (qs imposed : in m3/s
     * fixed value by keyword LEFT SOLID FLUX or by
     * additional column QS in LEFT BOUNDARY FILE)
  2: Homogeneous Neumann (null gradients)
  3: Periodic
  4: Equilibrium slope (qs = f(Jeq))
  5: Dirichlet (qs computed from hydro cdl values)

  RIGHT SOLID FLUX [float]                           : 0.
  Code variable: qsb
  Imposed solid flux qs (for Dirichlet condition: 1)
  solid discharge in m3/s

  RIGHT EQUILIBRIUM SLOPE [float]                    : 0.005
  Code variable: Jeqb
  Imposed equilibrium slope Jep (for bnd condition :4)
  
  BEDLOAD FORMULA [int]                              : 1
  Code variable: bedload_formula
  1: Grass (1981)
  2: Grass Modified
  3: Meyer-Peter and Muller (1948)
  4: Standardized MPM, Zanke and Roland (2020)
  5: Lefort (2014)
  6: Recking (2013)
  7: Recking (2015)
  8: Engelund and Hansen (1967)
  9: Van Rijn (1984)

  BEDLOAD CALIBRATION COEFFICIENT [float]            : 1.
  Code variable: bedload_coef
  Coefficient to calibrate bedload flux qs

  GRASS AG [float]                                   : 0.001
  Code variable: Ag
  GRASS MG [float] 1<=mg<=4                          : 3.
  Code variable: mg
  
  CRITICAL SHIELDS [float]                           : 0.047
  Code variable: tau_c
  - if == 0.: computed in Arrakis as a function of d50
  - if != 0.: user defined constant value
  
  STD MPM COEF A [float]                             : 10.24
  Code variable: smpm_a
  STD MPM COEF B [float]                             : 0.7
  Code variable: smpm_b

  SLOPE DIFFUSION [bool]                             : yes
  Code variable: diffusion_z
  SLOPE DIFFUSION COEFFICIENT [float]                : 1.E-3
  Code variable: nu_z
  SLOPE CRITICAL THRESHOLD [float]                   : 1.
  Code variable: slope_cr

  NON ERODIBLE BED DAMPING REGION DEPTH [float]      : 0.1
  Code variable: eps_b
  Depth of the damping region
  =0.: set to 10% of min(zb-zf)
  >0.: set to the specified value

  BED FRICTION SCALING COEFFICIENT [float]           : 1.
  Code variable: bed_fric_coef
  Coefficient to scale friction in bedload shear stress


#====================================================#
ADVANCED NUMERICAL PARAMETERS:
#====================================================#

  UNLOCK ADVANCED PARAMETERS [bool]                  : no
  Code variable: advanced_params

  RECONSTRUCTION METHOD [int]                        : 2
  Code variable: rec_method
  1: gradient
  2: variables

  H FLUX LIMITER [int]                               : 1
  Code variable: muscl_ilim_h
  1: Min Mod
  2: Van Albada
  3: Van Leer
  4: MC
  5: Super Bee
  6: Generalized Min Mod

  U FLUX LIMITER [int]                               : 1
  Code variable: muscl_ilim_u
  T FLUX LIMITER [int]                               : 1
  Code variable: muscl_ilim_t

  HYDROSTATIC RECONSTRUCTION [int]                   : 1
  Code variable: hydrostarec
  0: No reconstructions
  1: Audusse and al. (default for SV)
  2: Chen and Noelle
  3: Centered 
  4: Centered Roe (default for ROE-SVE)
  5: Upwind Roe (Vazquez-Cendon)

  BOTTOM FRICTION SCHEME [int]                       : 3
  Code variable: frict_scheme
  1: Explicit (unstable)
  2: Semi-implicit
  3: implicit

  VARIABLE WIDTH SCHEME [int]                        : 2
  Code variable: width_scheme
  1: 1st order FD (upwind, experimental) 
  2: 2nd order FD (Centered, default for HLL, ACU)
  3: 3rd order FD (experimental)
  4: 4th order FD (only for constant dx, experimental)
  5: Upwind Roe (Vazquez-Cendon, default for ROE)

  SVE WAVES APPROXIMATION [int]                      : 1
  Code variable: swe_roots_approx
  1: Cardano's method (default with ROE-SVE)
  2: Soares-Frazao and Zech approximation (default with HLL-SVE)
  3: Nickalls' approximation (default with ACU-SVE)

  BEDLOAD FLUX DERIVATIVES [int]                     : 0
  Code variable: qs_derivatives
  0: exact formula
  1: finite differences (forward)
  2: finite differences (backward)
  3: finite differences (centered)
  4: finite differences (optim)

  BEDLOAD FLUX DERIVATIVES STEP FOR H [float]        : 1.E-5
  Code variable: qs_derivatives_dh
  dh increment for finite difference flux derivative

  BEDLOAD FLUX DERIVATIVES STEP FOR U [float]        : 1.E-5
  Code variable: qs_derivatives_du
  du increment for finite difference flux derivative

  NON ERODIBLE BED FLUX LIMITER [int]                : 1
  Code variable: qs_lim
  0: no qs limitor
  1: add qs limitor to prevent zb<zf

  NON ERODIBLE BED DAMPING REGION [int]              : 1
  Code variable: eps_b_damping
  0: no damping of qs
  1: qs = psi*qs if 0<zb-zf<eps_b with 0<psi<1

  SUSPENSION TAU SCHEME [int]                        : 1
  Code variable: susp_taus_scheme
  0: centered scheme
  1: upwind scheme (Fr)

  SUSPENSION TRACER TIME SCHEME [int]                : 0
  Code variable: susp_trac_scheme
  0: explicit
  1: implicit

  STEADY SOLVER PRECISION [float]                    : 1.E-8
  Code variable: std_precision
  Precision of the steady non-linear iterative solver (Newton)

  STEADY SOLVER MAXIMUM ITERATIONS [int]             : 50
  Code variable: std_max_iter
  Maximum number of iteration for the steady non-linear 
  iterative solver (Newton)

  STEADY SOLVER FROUDE IN CRITICAL ZONES [float]     : 0.9
  Code variable: std_critical_fr
  Froude number for the h clipping in critical zones

  STEADY SOLVER CRITICAL OPTION [int]                : 0
  Code variable: std_critical_opt
  Option for the computation of critical zones in steady solver
  0: left subcritical state computed with closest critical node
  1: left subcritical state computed with last subcritical node
